# Delivery workflow

- For nontrivial interactive work, state the user-visible goal, acceptance
  criteria, constraints, and non-goals before editing.
- Inspect existing code, tests, rules, skills, and relevant MCP tools before
  assuming behavior is missing.
- Keep changes narrowly scoped; record adjacent issues instead of silently
  expanding the task.
- Use Laravel Boost for version-aware Laravel documentation and application
  inspection when relevant.
- Prefer tests that assert externally observable behavior.
- Interactive agents: run the narrowest relevant check while iterating and
  `./scripts/verify.sh` before completion.
- Approved Cursor Automations named in `AGENTS.md` (**Add test coverage**,
  **Generate docs**): run scoped checks, record results in the PR, and treat CI
  failures on the automation PR as blockers. **Summarize changes daily** is
  Git/GitHub read-only.
- Treat test, lint, type, build, route, or migration failures as blockers unless
  they are proven pre-existing and reported clearly. Report automation failures;
  do not bypass quality gates.
- Repository-approved Cursor Automations may commit, push, and open/update PRs
  as scoped in `AGENTS.md`. All other agents: do not commit, push, merge,
  deploy, access production, or install/authenticate tools without explicit
  user approval. No agent or automation may merge, deploy, force-push, skip
  hooks, or access production without a separate explicit human decision.
